senses.gloss:
(IV)--one of the nine planets; son of Soma (moon) [त्विषि (वा। प्।)] and तारा wife of बृहस्पति; known as राजपुत्र; of brown colour; has a lustrous white chariot drawn by ten horses of different colours; originator of the हस्तिशास्त्र; and learned in the अर्थशास्त्र; got the kingdom on the earth;
1: M. २४. 3-१०; ९३. १०, १७; ११५. 1; १२७. 1-3; वा. ५२. ७२; Vi. I. 8. ११; IV. 6. ३२-34.
occupies a position above (below वि। प्।) that of शुक्र; generally good and benevolent; but when separated from the sun preced- ing him, he causes showers or draughts;
2: भा. V. २२. १३; M. २६४. 8; Vi. II. 7. 8.
enamoured of the figure of इला (इला converted into the other sex at शरवण); in the guise of a Brahmana, he approached her; she consented to be his wife on his saying that he was Budha; father of Pururavas; Rajaputraka Aila;
3: भा IX. 1. ३४-5; १४. १४-15; Br. II. २४. ४९-134; III. 3. २३; ६५. ४४; ६६. 1; M. ११. ५४; १२. १४.
in the chariot of Tripura;
4: Ib. १२८. ४८, ६५; १३३. २०.
at the bottom of all ताराग्रहस्;
5: वा. १०१. १३२.
with the प्रकृति of नारायण; in extent three-fourths of Kuja and Saura; has eight rays; lies above the नक्षत्रस्;
6: Ib. ५३. ३१, ६७, ८७ and ९७.
above २००,000 yojanas from the constellar regions;
7: Vi. II. 7. 7.
chariot of, made of wind and fire and drawn by eight horses;
8: Ib. II. १२. १८.
Sudhyumna, son of Manu, cursed by शिव, became a woman on whom Budha begot Pururavas.
9: Ib. IV. 1. ११-12; वा. ८५. १७.
